Bursa Note — clean-room notice (competitor-inspired analytics)
================================================================

Bursa Note's position-cycle engine, Edge Dialect composite, statement
importers, and excursion estimates were independently implemented by the
Bursa team from first principles and public trading mathematics
(FIFO/LIFO/average-cost lot matching, standard drawdown and expectancy
definitions).

During research we studied the public behavior and documentation of
several open-source journals, including LuxAlgo trade-journal (MIT).
No source lines, comments, test fixtures, or sample files were copied.
Identifier names, file layout, thresholds, and weights are original to
Bursa; where mechanics necessarily coincide (flat-to-flat cycles must
split flat-crossing fills; any composite must normalize components),
expression and calibration differ — see
Documentation/Engineering/Note/BURSA-EDGE-DIALECT.md and the
scripts/cleanroom-diff.mjs spot-check.

Third-party open-source software actually vendored or depended upon is
listed in package.json / pnpm-lock.yaml with its own license terms.
